    ownerNotes: "Added at the owner's instruction (September 2026). Research notes: Pentair's commercial pool page URL slug reads '340-series-and-410-series' while the page title reads '3800 Series'; ASC's older 'Commercial Aquatics' PDF is named 340-END-SUCTION.pdf. Pentair does not state on the fetched pages that the 340 Series was superseded by the 3800 Series, so no supersession claim is made. The 150 HP / 8,000 GPM figures on the pool page describe the combined 3800 + 410 offering, not the 3800 Series alone (brochure: 4,200 GPM). Pool-page feature 'Models rated to 100 ft TDH' and 'Cast Iron Bronze Fitted Models' are quoted as written; the pool brochure's material table shows stainless-fitted construction. Family image on the Aurora brand page is an alternative: /content/dam/extranet/nam/industrial-flow-technologies/flow/ift-image-library/aurora/end-suction-pumps/aurora-3800-series-single-stage-end-suction-pumps-family.png.",
